# WhatsappBot environment (copy to `.env` and fill in secrets).
# This file documents optional / scheduled features; not all vars are required.

# Owner WhatsApp number (digits or full JID). Required for cron jobs that notify you.
# MY_PHONE=
# SECOND_PHONE=

# --- agent-runner (out-of-process Claude agent, docs/adr/0001-agent-runner-out-of-process.md) ---
# Every `claude…` message (after the allowlist check) is forwarded to agent-runner's localhost API,
# and `!restart` refuses while a runner run is active. The Claude pipeline, the cron issue tracer
# and their settings (workspaces, post-run flags, pause, model) live in agent-runner's `.env`.
# The bot delivers the runner's Redis Stream outbox (`agent-runner:outbox`, via REDIS_URL),
# merging whatever is waiting into one message per chat. Messages that arrived while the bot was
# down aren't replayed: you get one "you missed N" line, and `claude:missed` lists them.
# Default http://127.0.0.1:3790.
# AGENT_RUNNER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3790
# How often the outbox is polled, in ms. Default 5000.
# AGENT_RUNNER_OUTBOX_POLL_MS=5000
# Redis for the outbox cursor (and CHAT_MEMORY_BACKEND=redis, if enabled). Default redis://127.0.0.1:6379.
# REDIS_URL=redis://127.0.0.1:6379

# --- Reddit-bot daily cron digest (issue #61) ---
# Companion: reddit-bot `npm run cron_digest` writes reports/daily-cron-status.txt
# (~02:45 UTC). WhatsappBot polls from REDDIT_CRON_DIGEST_HOUR_UTC and sends once
# the file is fresh and stamped for today's UTC day. Missing/stale alerts fire at
# most once/day and do not block a later digest send when the file arrives.
# Schedule is UTC to match reddit-bot user crontab (CRON_TZ=UTC).
# REDDIT_BOT_STATUS_FILE=/home/alexis/Projects/reddit-bot/reports/daily-cron-status.txt
# REDDIT_CRON_DIGEST_HOUR_UTC=3
# REDDIT_CRON_DIGEST_MINUTE_UTC=0
# REDDIT_CRON_DIGEST_POLL_MS=60000
# REDDIT_CRON_DIGEST_DISABLE=1
# REDDIT_CRON_DIGEST_ALSO_SECOND_PHONE=1
# REDDIT_CRON_DIGEST_LAST_SENT_FILE=/home/alexis/Projects/WhatsappBot/logs/claude-agent/reddit-cron-digest-last-sent.json
# (default kept under logs/claude-agent/ for continuity; deleting that folder only resets this marker)

# --- Home manuals Q&A (issue #98) ---
# Base URL of the home-manuals service (alexisNorthcoders/home-manuals). `home <question>`
# and natural-language home questions (routed through homeAgent) POST { question } to
# `${HOME_MANUALS_URL}/ask` and expect { answer, sources } back. Unset: the `home` command
# explains it's not configured, and homeAgent skips (falls through to normal chat) silently.
# HOME_MANUALS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3100
# Always route through homeAgent, bypassing the keyword gate (debugging only).
# HOME_AGENT_ALWAYS=1

# --- Scheduled reminders / nudge me (issues #64–#68) ---
# Relative/absolute “remind me / nudge me …” — allowlisted actors only.
# Store is local JSON (survives restarts). Poller delivers due reminders into the origin chat.
# On reconnect the scheduler runs an immediate catch-up tick so overdue reminders
# from downtime are delivered promptly (marked “late” when >2 minutes overdue).
# Delivery uses pending → delivering → fired with deliveryAttemptAt + a
# process-local in-flight marker so long sends are never settled as fired early.
# Only known pre-send failures release back to pending; uncertain post-send
# errors finalize as fired (at-most-once, no duplicate retry).
# Safety (#68): text truncation, pending-per-chat cap, optional horizon, terminal prune.
# REMINDERS_STORE_FILE=/home/alexis/Projects/WhatsappBot/logs/reminders/reminders.json
# REMINDERS_POLL_MS=30000
# REMINDERS_DISABLE=1
# REMINDERS_MAX_TEXT_CHARS=500
# REMINDERS_MAX_PENDING_PER_CHAT=25
# REMINDERS_MAX_HORIZON_DAYS=365
# REMINDERS_TERMINAL_RETENTION_MS=604800000
# REMINDERS_MAX_TERMINAL=200
